 60CR c  Intermediate energy Coulomb excitation                                 
 60CR c  Secondary cocktail beam produced in fragmentation of 130 MeV/nucleon   
 60CR2c  {+76}Ge beam on a 423 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target followed by selection    
 60CR3c  and purification using A1900 separator at NSCL facility. Scattered     
 60CR4c  particles were identified on an event-by-event basis through time-of-  
 60CR5c  flight and energy loss measurements by S-800 ionization chamber and    
 60CR6c  plastic scintillation detectors. Gamma-rays were detected in           
 60CR7c  coincidence with scattered {+60}Cr projectiles using SeGA array of     
 60CR8c  17, 32-fold segmented Ge detectors surrounding the Coulomb excitation  
 60CR9c  target in front of the S800 spectrograph. Measured Coulomb excitation  
 60CRAc  cross sections and deduced B(E2) values using Winther-Alder theory.    
